{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You are sons.</b> This pericope is juxtaposed here to warn them not to gash yourselves, because there may be among the dead of a seduced city a father or son or brother or any close relative." "<b>You are sons to HaShem your Elohim.</b> Therefore do not gash yourselves over what befalls you — even if you do not understand why such a thing happened to you. Rather, rely on Him, for all the deeds of HaShem are for the good — like small children who do not understand their father's deeds but rely on him." "<b>And you shall not make a baldness between your eyes for the dead.</b> If your father dies, do not gash yourselves and do not make a baldness, and do not mourn excessively, for you are not thereby orphans, since you have a great father — alive and enduring — HaShem. And furthermore, you are a holy people and are not permitted to disfigure yourself."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:43.873188953Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}